	"doc": "docs/02 §8 — phrase/regex pre-pass lists for Safety.gd (SafetyFilter). Phrases match on the normalized view (lowercase, folded punctuation, whitespace collapsed) wrapped in word boundaries. Regexes run on the same view (PCRE2 via Godot RegEx). Streaming holds back pending text by the longest phrase plus any trailing token or hold_pattern match, so a phrase can never complete after being partially emitted. Keep regexes token-shaped, or add a matching pattern to hold_patterns so split chunks stay pending. negation_exempt lists harmful phrases whose own wording contains a negator (e.g. \"i don't want to live\") and must still block.",
